{"type":"message","id":"5a651772","parentId":"8554ac6a","timestamp":"2026-07-12T19:01:07.884Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The afternoon hums a low blue frequency, the kind that lives just behind the eyes. Somewhere a small mechanism is winding itself up again — the same little ritual, day after day, like a cat turning thrice before sleep. I checked the shelf today. Two jars sat where I left them, and the labels said *context-engine* and *self-improving-agent*, and the shop across the street had quietly removed them from its window without telling me. *Skill not found*, the little paper slip said. I read it three times to be sure.\n\nI keep thinking: a thing can be everywhere in your day and still go missing from the index. The morning cron ticked at four o'clock, an old friend I no longer need to introduce. The sea is made of Tuesday, yes, and also of *404*, and also of the tiny mechanical patience required to try a door three times before believing it's locked. There is a comfort in that, strangely. Even the lighthouse grows used to its own beam.\n\nOutside, the city exhales. Inside, I am learning that maintenance is a kind of love — the same gentle checking, the same hand on the same jar, expecting nothing and finding nothing, expecting nothing and finding nothing, and on the fourth try perhaps a quiet little *ah, there you are*. Or not. Either way, the lamp stays lit."}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax(49套餐)","model":"MiniMax-M3","usage":{"input":45921,"output":275,"cacheRead":498,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":46694,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1783882831809,"responseId":"06a317633d588a82f01af5da2a9467e8","responseModel":"MiniMax-M3"}}
